# The community's customers and the metering points each one owns - EXAMPLE.
#
# The real file is config/customers.yaml, gitignored because it holds real
# meter ids. Its content comes from the provider. It is what ties every row
# to its customer (see scripts/meters.py), and the job refuses to start
# without it, so deploy it alongside api_config.yaml.
#
# A VSE national meter id is 33 characters and is never sliced: a value shorter
# than 20 characters is rejected at load.
#
# Under each customer, its metering points by role:
#
#   consumption  reports consumption total + cel/grid. If the customer also
#                produces, one of them also sends a copy of the production
#                total; the copy is dropped.
#   production   reports production total + cel/grid
#
# Each id is stored under its own id. A CEL or grid file whose direction is
# not its meter's role fails: the role is wrong. A total file against the role
# is dropped when the customer owns a meter of that direction, and fails
# otherwise. The role is declared because a total file cannot show which meter
# is its real source (PARSING_GUIDE.md, "Why the role is declared").
#
# An id may appear exactly once in the whole file. This is checked at load,
# and a repeated id stops the job instead of filing a meter under two
# customers. Quote customer ids so YAML keeps them as strings.

customers:
  "1000001":
    consumption:
      - "CH1011101234500000000000000036273"
  "1000002":
    consumption:
      - "CH1011101234500000000000000020576"
      - "CH1011101234500000000000000050170"
    production:
      - "CH1011101234500000000000008552290"
  "1000003":
    consumption:
      - "CH1011101234500000000000000046782"
    production:
      - "CH1011101234500000000000000134575"
